      "confidence": 0.9,
      "evidence": [
        "artifacts/ae_tpd_by_year.csv shows A/E oscillating between 0.61 and 1.65 across all 10 years with no sustained directional trend",
        "empirical year-to-year SD of A/E (~0.34) is an order of magnitude larger than the Poisson expectation (1/sqrt(E) ≈ 0.035) given expected annual claim counts of 400–1100"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate source of extreme dispersion: verify data integrity (e.g., accident vs policy year mix, reporting lags, large single-account/group claims), review changes in benefit design or underwriting standards, and assess whether expected values are miscalibrated. Hold pricing/valuation adjustments until volatility driver is identified."
    }
  ]
}

